DECISIONS 284, WIRE.md §5.11: a stored method returning its own receiver has no finite wire for `emit json` (a stack overflow of the build before): the json variant, from check, at the fn.
-- a/a.canon --
package a

/// A node.
record Node {
  /// Its key.
  id: String

  /// Itself.
  export fn me(self) -> Node { return self }
}

/// The nodes.
let nodes: [Node] keyed by id = [{ id: "x" }]

emit json { out: "out/" }
-- findings.txt --
error[E8019]  a/a.canon:9:13
  emit json cannot generate a by-value cycle of records through a stored method result; return a ref to the record instead

1 error, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
